---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Cpu, Download, HardDrive, Gift, Info } from '@lucide/astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Setup', href: '/setup' },
  { label: 'ROMs' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Getting ROMs"
  description="To run a real C64 or Amiga, you need the machine's system ROMs. Here's why, and how to get them legally — for free where you can, and cheaply where you can't."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <div class="roms-page">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-content">
        <div class="hero-icon-wrapper">
          <Cpu size={44} class="hero-icon" />
        </div>
        <h1>A note on ROMs</h1>
        <p class="hero-subtitle">What you need to run a real C64 or Amiga — and how to get it honestly</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The why -->
    <section class="prose-section">
      <div class="container">
        <p>
          To run anything on a C64 or an Amiga — real or emulated — you need the machine's
          <strong>system ROMs</strong>: the built-in software (KERNAL and BASIC on the C64;
          Kickstart and Workbench on the Amiga) that makes the machine a machine. An emulator
          without them is an empty shell.
        </p>
        <p>
          Here's the honest part. <strong>This course is free, and always will be — but the ROMs
          aren't ours to give away.</strong> They're still
          <a href="/vault/distribution/abandonware">owned</a> (today, by a company called
          <a href="/vault/companies/cloanto">Cloanto</a>, who've kept these platforms legally alive
          for decades), and we're not going to hand out
          copies of someone else's work to save you a step. Preserving these machines
          <em>properly</em> — with respect for the people and the history behind them — is the
          whole point of this project. Quietly pirating the ROMs would rather undercut that.
        </p>
        <p>
          So you'll bring your own. It's cheaper and easier than it sounds, you only do it once,
          and below is exactly how for your machine.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- C64 -->
    <section class="platform-section alt" id="commodore-64">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Getting your C64 ROMs</h2>
        <p class="section-description">Pick whichever fits you:</p>

        <div class="options">
          <div class="option">
            <div class="option-head">
              <Download size={20} class="option-icon" />
              <h3>Want it to just work? — C64 Forever</h3>
              <span class="tag tag-recommended">Recommended</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              Cloanto's <a href="https://www.c64forever.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">C64 Forever</a>
              (Plus edition, ~$10) gives you every official ROM, legally, in a couple of clicks. The
              simplest path if you don't have real hardware — and you're buying from the people who
              preserved them.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="option">
            <div class="option-head">
              <HardDrive size={20} class="option-icon" />
              <h3>Own a real C64?</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              Dump the KERNAL, BASIC and character ROMs from it — they're already yours. We'll point
              you at a tool.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="option">
            <div class="option-head">
              <Gift size={20} class="option-icon" />
              <h3>Want it completely free? — OpenROMs</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              The community's open-source KERNAL/BASIC replacements
              (<a href="https://github.com/MEGA65/open-roms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenROMs</a>)
              are free to use. Great for the <strong>assembly</strong> track — but their BASIC isn't
              finished, so the <strong>BASIC</strong> lessons will hit gaps. Use OpenROMs for
              assembly; use a real BASIC ROM for the BASIC track.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Amiga -->
    <section class="platform-section" id="commodore-amiga">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Getting your Amiga ROMs</h2>
        <p class="section-description">The Amiga needs <strong>Kickstart</strong> (its boot ROM) and <strong>Workbench</strong> (its desktop):</p>

        <div class="options">
          <div class="option">
            <div class="option-head">
              <Download size={20} class="option-icon" />
              <h3>Want it to just work? — Amiga Forever</h3>
              <span class="tag tag-recommended">Recommended</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              Cloanto's <a href="https://www.amigaforever.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Amiga Forever</a>
              (Plus edition, ~€40) gives you every Kickstart version plus Workbench, legally and
              reliably. For most learners without real hardware this is the path — and it's the exact
              setup this course is built and tested against.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="option">
            <div class="option-head">
              <HardDrive size={20} class="option-icon" />
              <h3>Own a real Amiga?</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              Dump your Kickstart ROM from it — it's yours.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="option">
            <div class="option-head">
              <Gift size={20} class="option-icon" />
              <h3>The free option, honestly — AROS</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              There's a free, open Kickstart replacement
              (<a href="https://aros.sourceforge.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AROS</a>). It's
              genuinely clever, but it can't boot Workbench 3.1 and many programs won't run on it, so
              it won't carry you through this track. We mention it for honesty, not as the route we'd
              point you to.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ROM handling note -->
    <section class="prose-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="callout">
          <Info size={20} class="callout-icon" />
          <p>
            <strong>How the lessons handle ROMs:</strong> we do not redistribute commercial system
            ROMs. C64 assembly can use open ROMs where the emulator supports them; Amiga and C64
            BASIC need ROMs you provide to your local emulator.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Back Link -->
    <section class="back-section">
      <div class="container back-links">
        <a href="/setup" class="back-link">&larr; Back to Setup Guide</a>
        <a href="/commodore-64" class="start-link">Start the C64 Curriculum &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .roms-page {
    --accent-color: var(--color-house-2);
  }

  /* Hero — paper/ink, matching the synthesis direction */
  .hero {
    text-align: center;
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4) var(--space-8);
  }

  .hero-content {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .hero-icon-wrapper {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .hero-icon {
    color: var(--color-house-2);
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-family-read);
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.9;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3) 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .hero-subtitle {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.2vw, 1.2rem);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Sections */
  .container {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .prose-section {
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-4);
  }

  .platform-section {
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4);
    background: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .platform-section.alt {
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
  }

  .prose-section p,
  .platform-section p {
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4) 0;
  }

  .prose-section a,
  .platform-section a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 2px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-primary) 30%, transparent 70%);
  }

  .prose-section a:hover,
  .platform-section a:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .platform-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2) 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .section-description {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary) !important;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6) !important;
  }

  /* Option blocks */
  .options {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .option {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-6);
  }

  .option-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .option-head h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .option-icon {
    color: var(--ink);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .option p {
    margin: 0 !important;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary) !important;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .tag {
    font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    border: 1px solid currentColor;
  }

  /* Accessible success green per theme — the semantic --color-success (#22c55e)
     is too light for small text on the light surface. */
  .tag-recommended {
    color: #166534;
    margin-left: auto;
  }

  :global(:root[data-theme="dark"]) .tag-recommended {
    color: #4ade80;
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :global(:root:not([data-theme])) .tag-recommended {
      color: #4ade80;
    }
  }

  /* Callout */
  .callout {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-6);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-house-2);
  }

  .callout-icon {
    color: var(--color-house-2);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
  }

  .callout p {
    margin: 0 !important;
    color: var(--color-text) !important;
  }

  /* Back Section */
  .back-section {
    padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .back-links {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .back-link, .start-link {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .back-link:hover, .start-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .back-links {
      flex-direction: column;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .tag-recommended {
      margin-left: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
